WEBVTT

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.920
Go ahead Scott. Yeah I think it's very

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:07.160
worthwhile reflecting just for a moment

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:10.280
on when we say public private yes the

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:11.719
partnerships implicit but there's

00:00:11.719 --> 00:00:13.160
actually a partnership within the

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:15.959
private sector. So many many companies

00:00:15.959 --> 00:00:17.319
especially owners of critical

00:00:17.319 --> 00:00:20.120
infrastructure they outsource or they

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:23.079
purchase cyber security services from a

00:00:23.079 --> 00:00:25.880
cyber security vendor or

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:28.760
company. Now this is also a very

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:30.599
important area for us to reflect on when

00:00:30.599 --> 00:00:32.120
we think about critical infrastructure

00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:35.479
because um many of you and I put my hand

00:00:35.479 --> 00:00:37.640
up who was impacted by the crowd strike

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:40.920
IT outage last year. Any hand. the crowd

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:43.319
strike out the blue screen popped up

00:00:43.319 --> 00:00:45.000
flights around the world were cancelled

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.359
or delayed so that wasn't a hack that

00:00:48.359 --> 00:00:50.280
was an IT outage in that instance but

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:52.280
what it showed me as a cyber security

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:54.440
professional is that we have an

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:57.400
increasing what we call supply chain

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.880
risk or concentration risk within the

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:02.359
supply chain now all owners of critical

00:01:02.359 --> 00:01:03.880
infrastructure whether you're in energy

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:06.839
or water or aviation or whatever if we

00:01:06.839 --> 00:01:09.319
all use that one vendor then that's a

00:01:09.319 --> 00:01:10.359
concentration

00:01:10.359 --> 00:01:12.359
risk right because if that vendor goes

00:01:12.359 --> 00:01:14.839
down then all of us are hit. So what

00:01:14.839 --> 00:01:16.520
that incident showed me is that we need

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:19.639
to be very aware of not only within this

00:01:19.639 --> 00:01:21.719
private partner uh p public private

00:01:21.719 --> 00:01:23.959
partnerships there are many private

00:01:23.959 --> 00:01:25.879
owners of critical infrastructure who

00:01:25.879 --> 00:01:29.560
depend increasingly on these vendors but

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:32.040
how do we keep a check on the vendors

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:34.040
because remember I mentioned the first

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:35.800
panel I was on there's a regulatory

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:38.120
conflict of interest between regulators

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:40.679
and industry but likewise there is a

00:01:40.679 --> 00:01:42.840
commercial conflict of interest when it

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:45.080
comes to the provision of cyber security

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:46.760
services to critical infrastructure

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:49.800
owners. I'll give you a great example.

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:52.360
In 2020, I was looking after I was

00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:53.800
running threat intelligence fusion

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:55.320
operations for the world's biggest

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:57.560
finance sector, ISAC, threat

00:01:57.560 --> 00:01:59.879
intelligence sharing community, FS ISAC.

00:01:59.879 --> 00:02:02.120
And what we observed in 2020 was an

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:04.280
incident that first impacted the Reserve

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:06.280
Bank of New Zealand and then the

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:08.520
Australian corporate regulator ASICH.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:10.120
Now what was interesting with this is

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:12.919
that the the vector of attack was a file

00:02:12.919 --> 00:02:15.399
transfer appliance which was run by a

00:02:15.399 --> 00:02:18.200
company called Ailion. Now Ailion is a

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:19.800
company that is a private company

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:21.240
registered on the New York Stock

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:24.440
Exchange. What do you think is the main

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:27.639
incentive of the uh executives who are

00:02:27.639 --> 00:02:30.360
on the board of Syilian? It's profit

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:33.000
isn't it? Profit is what drives a

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:34.360
corporation that's listed on the

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:35.879
exchange and the share price

00:02:35.879 --> 00:02:38.280
performance. Now the commercial conflict

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:40.040
of interest that I'm referring to with

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:42.120
vendors of all technology not just cyber

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:44.360
security vendors is that it's in their

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:47.240
own selfish interest to under reportport

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:50.840
an incident. Now if as a supply chain uh

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:53.080
provider they have their footprint in

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:55.399
many many sectors many many types of

00:02:55.399 --> 00:02:57.399
critical infrastructure that's not a

00:02:57.399 --> 00:02:59.800
good conflict of interest to have as a

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:01.639
critical infrastructure owner because

00:03:01.639 --> 00:03:04.520
they are actually incentivized not to be

00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:06.520
fast and not to be complete in the

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:08.840
information they share to me. So how do

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:12.200
we control for this increasing supply

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:14.040
chain risk that we have from our

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:16.120
vendors? Well, the way we are going to

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:17.320
do that in Australia and I hope

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:19.639
Indonesia can do the same is that you

00:03:19.639 --> 00:03:21.800
unite the people who own the critical

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:23.399
infrastructure and you say look the

00:03:23.399 --> 00:03:26.760
better we all here share information

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:29.320
okay the more we will detect and

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:32.280
identify when a vendor is compromised

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:33.800
because we shouldn't wait for the vendor

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:35.320
to be honest because they have a

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:37.399
commercial conflict of interest. So by

00:03:37.399 --> 00:03:39.159
collective intelligence sharing within

00:03:39.159 --> 00:03:41.240
our community, it's not only good to

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:43.800
keep the bad guys, the hackers away,

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:46.120
it's also a mechanism, a practical

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:48.680
operational mechanism that enables us to

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:50.919
keep a track of our supply chain risks

00:03:50.919 --> 00:03:52.919
and threats through, you know, through

00:03:52.919 --> 00:03:54.280
the sharing of information. And I think

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:55.720
that's very important because it's a

00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:59.000
balance of power. No individual single

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:00.680
part of the economy should have total

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:02.440
control. There needs to be a

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:04.120
distribution of power with checks and

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:06.040
balances. And that's what a mechanism

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:09.000
like a CIS sack for a country can do is

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:11.399
it helps on this concentration risk in

00:04:11.399 --> 00:04:13.560
that public private bit is the private

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:15.400
private bit. Right. Yeah. Yeah. It's
